+## ms-format-unit
+
+The API provides a unit option to format and numeric ms calls: unit?: 'ms' | 's' | 'm' | 'h' | 'd' | 'w' | 'mo' | 'y'. When set, always format in that unit using the existing unit conversion constants, Math.round(value / unitSize), and the existing short/long style and pluralization threshold (absolute input >= 1.5 units). Milliseconds preserve the numeric value without rounding as before. The default automatic unit choice is unchanged. Validate unknown runtime unit values with an Error, without requiring any subtype or message. String parsing paths and parseStrict remain unchanged and do not apply formatting options. Export the options type, keep overload return types, and generate usable public declarations. Document forced units with short/long examples.
